class.description:
Extend this class to integrate a custom 3D upscaler (for example DLSS, XeSS, FSR 3 or later, or your own neural network) with the Forward+ renderer, without modifying the engine. Assign an instance to [member Viewport.scaling_3d_custom_upscaler] and set [member Viewport.scaling_3d_mode] to [constant Viewport.SCALING_3D_MODE_CUSTOM], or use [member ProjectSettings.rendering/scaling_3d/custom_upscaler_class] for the root viewport.
The renderer draws the scene at the reduced internal resolution with sub-pixel camera jitter and motion vectors, then calls [method _upscale] once per view. The implementation reads the textures from [RenderingUpscaleParameters] and records its work with the [RenderingDevice] returned by [method RenderingServer.get_rendering_device], writing the result to [method RenderingUpscaleParameters.get_output].
Upscalers that must call into a native SDK can return [code]true[/code] from [method _uses_native_commands]. [method _record_native_commands] is then called with the native command buffer while the frame is recorded, and the renderer takes care of the barriers of all textures in [RenderingUpscaleParameters]. Native texture handles can be obtained with [method RenderingDevice.get_driver_resource].
[codeblock]
extends RenderingUpscaler

var shader: RID
var pipeline: RID
var sampler: RID

func _get_upscaler_name():
    return "Bilinear example"

func _is_supported():
    return RenderingServer.get_rendering_device() != null

func _upscale(parameters):
    var rd = RenderingServer.get_rendering_device()
    if not shader.is_valid():
        pass # Compile the compute shader, create the pipeline and sampler here.
    var color = RDUniform.new()
    color.uniform_type = RenderingDevice.UNIFORM_TYPE_SAMPLER_WITH_TEXTURE
    color.binding = 0
    color.add_id(sampler)
    color.add_id(parameters.get_color())
    var output = RDUniform.new()
    output.uniform_type = RenderingDevice.UNIFORM_TYPE_IMAGE
    output.binding = 1
    output.add_id(parameters.get_output())
    var uniform_set = UniformSetCacheRD.get_cache(shader, 0, [color, output])
    var size = parameters.get_target_size()
    var list = rd.compute_list_begin()
    rd.compute_list_bind_compute_pipeline(list, pipeline)
    rd.compute_list_bind_uniform_set(list, uniform_set, 0)
    rd.compute_list_dispatch(list, (size.x + 7) / 8, (size.y + 7) / 8, 1)
    rd.compute_list_end()

func _notification(what):
    if what == NOTIFICATION_PREDELETE and shader.is_valid():
        var rd = RenderingServer.get_rendering_device()
        rd.free_rid(sampler)
        rd.free_rid(shader) # Also frees the pipeline.
[/codeblock]
[b]Note:[/b] Custom upscalers are only available in the Forward+ renderer. When an upscaler isn't assigned or [method is_supported] returns [code]false[/code], the viewport falls back to FSR 2.
